\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Full spectrograms (0--8~kHz) of one correctly produced token of each of the eight sounds (native ARCTIC voices, sentences not used for training), cut like an isolated word, with what the tool detected at the time of the evaluation: red lines mark the detected hiss (fricatives, /t\textesh /) or the burst and the start of voicing (stops), the shaded area is the VOT interval, the dashed line is the CoG, and the title gives the verdict and the value on which it rests. For /m/ and /n/ the recogniser's probability is shown. Tokens were chosen as the first correct verdict for each sound, excluding a verdict resting on a mis-located hiss (see Section~\ref {sec:disc}).}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
